 351	Our results suggest an approach to the problem from a different angle: we provide a ``gap preserving'' protocol, in the sense that the completeness-soundness gap is a polynomial function of the underlying promise gap of
 352	the Hamiltonian, but \emph{independent} of the system size
 353	$n$. However, this occurs at the cost of much longer messages --- polynomial instead of logarithmic. 
