 690	\paragraph{Organization of the paper.}
 691	In Section~\ref{sec:prelim} we introduce some notation used throughout
 692	as well as basic definitions of stabilizer codes and local
 693	Hamiltonians. In Section~\ref{sec:linearity}, we establish an important technical component of our results, the linearity test and its quantum
 694	analysis. We expand this into a two-prover self-test for the Pauli group on
 695	$n$-qubits in Section~\ref{sec:twoprover}, which forms the basis for our main result. In
 696	Section~\ref{sec:manyprovers} we extend this test to handle more than
 697	two provers and show how it can be combined with
 698	an energy measurement test to devise a game for the local
 699	Hamiltonian problem. In Section~\ref{sec:delegated} we
 700	discuss the application of our protocol to delegated computation. 
