1351	  Suppose given a strategy $(N,\ket{\psi}_{AB}$) for the players in the Pauli braiding test (Figure~\ref{fig:protocol2player}) with success probability $\omega^*_{\enc} - \eps$, for some $\eps>0$. Then
1352	  there exists a local isometry $\Phi = (\Phi^A:\mH_A\to\mH_{A'}\otimes \mH_{A''},\Phi^B:\mH_B\to\mH_{B'}\otimes \mH_{B''})$ such that 
1353	  $$\Tr\Big( \big(\bra{\EPR}_{A'B'}^{\otimes
1354	      n}\otimes \Id_{A''B''}\big)\,\big( \Phi^A \otimes \Phi^B(\ket{\psi}\bra{\psi}_{AB})\big)\big( \ket{\EPR}_{A'B'}^{\otimes n} \otimes \Id_{A''B''}\big) \Big) = 1 - O\big(\eps^{1/8}\big).$$
1355	\end{corollary}
