1357	By instantiating the anticommutation game $G_\ac$ used in the test with the Magic Square game we obtain a robust self-test for $n$ EPR pairs in which the optimal strategy only requires the use of $(n+1)$ EPR pairs and is accepted with probability $1$.\footnote{In fact, for the case of the Magic Square game it is not hard to see that there always exists an optimal strategy in the test using $\max(2,n)$ EPR pairs.}
